                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-percentage"></i></div>
                        <h4>@Localizer["Qualitative"]</h4>
                        <p>@Localizer["Achievement is entered directly as a percentage (0–100). Use this when progress is judged rather than counted — for example, 'training session 70% complete'."]</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="feature-item">
                        <div class="feature-icon"><i class="fas fa-sort-numeric-up"></i></div>
                        <h4>@Localizer["Quantitative"]</h4>
                        <p>@Localizer["Achievement is measured by counting physical units (beneficiaries, metres, households, etc.). Enter a quantity and the system calculates the percentage: Achievement % = (Quantity ÷ Phase Target) × 100."]</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning-box">
                    <div class="info-icon"><i class="fas fa-lock"></i></div>
                    <div class="info-content">
                        <h4>@Localizer["Phase Type Lock"]</h4>
                        <p>@Localizer["The measure type (Qualitative or Quantitative) is set by the first measure added to a phase and cannot be changed afterward. All subsequent measures in the same phase must use the same type. Delete all phase measures first if you need to switch types."]</p>
